   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Best wishes for 1928. I have had a bad breakdown from worry and overwork. Did those slowcoaches in <name type="geo" key="G_DEU_STUT">Stuttgart</name> not send <rs type="person" key="syke83">you</rs> <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">your copy</rs>
                        </seg> yet? If so, please <foreign xml:lang="fra">
                            <hi rend="underline">réclamez</hi>
                        </foreign> from <name type="person" key="goll91">M. Ivan Goll</name>, <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI_39">27 rue Jasmin, Passy, Paris.</name> He is their agent.</p> <closer>
                        <salute>sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1928-01-01">1.1.28</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>  <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Joyce had requested that a copy of Georg Goyert’s German translation of <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name>, published in October 1927 be sent from the publisher, Rhein Verlag (with an office in Stuttgart), to Sykes – see JJ’s postcards to Sykes of <rs type="letter" key="L_69554">23 November 1927</rs> and 29 November (<name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">LIII</name> 167, misdated as 19 November).</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
